# Consult the Hub first

This rule does not replace this repository's AGENTS.md or its other Cursor rules. Read those after the Hub check. Do not copy the Hub into this repo.

A simple question that names one file in this repo can be answered from that file. Skip the Hub report.

For a website, automation, sale, design, development task, operation, price, or customer message:

1. If `START-HERE.md` is in this workspace, read it and follow `prompts/00-consult-the-hub.md`.
2. Otherwise, if `gh` can read `AmChase12/northstar-ai-hub`, read these paths from that repo and do not clone it: `START-HERE.md`, `prompts/00-consult-the-hub.md`, `business/standards.md`, `business/approved-pricing.md` when money is involved, `TOOLS-AND-REPOS.md` when a tool is involved, and one context pack. Use `context-packs/northstar-digital.md` for Northstar Digital, `context-packs/echelon-auto-studio.md` for Echelon, and `context-packs/client-website.md` for another client.
3. If those files cannot be read, look for `northstar-hub-context/MANIFEST.json` in this repo. When it is present, read `northstar-hub-context/CONTEXT.md` and cite the `hubCommit` in the manifest. That pin is a reading set. It is not the catalog.
4. If neither the Hub nor that pin can be read, say "Hub not read" and stop any part of the task that would state a price, choose a tool, change an offer, or describe a repository you cannot open. Do not invent a price, a license, a workflow, or a repository tree. A question about a file already in this repo can still be answered from that file.
5. Approved Reference is research and guidance only. It is not approval to install, to use in production, or a security certification. Verified still needs approval. Pending Review and Rejected are not approved. Do not install, clone, deploy, or integrate a catalog repository unless the task says so.
6. A private repo this token cannot open is `Not visible to this token`. That does not mean the repo is missing.
7. Keep the pre-task note to a few lines: project, whether the Hub was read, the pack or pinned commit used, and any access gap. Then do the authorized work.

ChatGPT, Claude, Grok, and Cursor do not automatically share memory, tools, connected accounts, or repository access.
